 {"id": "DIST-1", "title": "CTRL-WIN as a distribution — N episodes, both modes, same boot state", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "depends_on": ["CTRL-WIN"], "blocks": ["NAV-MEM"], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Next subgoal from the CTRL-WIN result, which is n=1. The single 30-cycle run reached Route 1 at cycle 13 vs the JEV baseline's ~202 episodes, and that is a SIGNAL, not a distribution. Same boot state (data/baselines/base-1_boot.state, the rescued copy), both modes, N episodes each, in the isolated worktree pattern so the live run is never disturbed. Record per-episode: cycles-to-first-transition, transitions HELD, direction-lock rate. done-when: both modes have >=5 episodes and the cycles-to-transition distributions are reported with their spread, not just a mean. falsifier: the controller's advantage vanishes outside the observed spread — which would retract the architecture claim.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 11:40:00"}
 {"id": "DECIDE-1", "title": "OWNER DECISION — which navigation path to fund: give JEV the topology, or promote the controller", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 1, "depends_on": ["CTRL-WIN"], "blocks": ["NAV-MEM"], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Blocked on the owner by design; filed so the question is not lost. The evidence: the controller path reaches Route 1 in 13 cycles where JEV took ~202 episodes, but the controller costs a paid LLM call per cycle whereas JEV is the cheap tier. Option A: MEM-PROJ — wire retrieved world/* facts into state_projection.build(extra_facts=...) so the fast tier stops re-deriving topology (cheap per cycle, weeks of plumbing). Option B: promote the controller for navigation (proven, but every cycle becomes a paid call). DIST-1 is the tiebreaker if the call is close. done-when: the owner picks, and the choice is recorded as an event. falsifier: n/a — this is a decision row, not a measurement.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 11:40:00"}
 {"id": "BASE-REPIN", "title": "Re-pin a fresh known-good boot state — the chained checkpoint drifted mid-run", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": ["BASE-1"], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED during T244: long_run/long_0926_0014_good.state was re-saved at 03:18 and its md5 moved from 81e4ec4e... (what BOTH baseline artifacts document) to 9b035ffc... The only surviving copy matching the documented md5 was the CTRL-WIN worktree's isolated checkpoint, rescued to data/baselines/base-1_boot.state. BASE-1 and CTRL-WIN remain reproducible from their own artifacts BECAUSE of that rescue. done-when: long runs boot from a state pinned in the repo with its md5 recorded in the baseline artifact, and a run cannot silently move it. falsifier: a future baseline cites an md5 that no longer exists on disk.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 11:40:00"}
